       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the max standard dose. I can enter it now.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is the usual starting dose, and you can titrate up to 10 mg.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't controlling BP, an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is usually preferred over going above 10 mg.\n- **Amlodipine 20 mg is intentional.** If you want exactly this dose, for example because of a specialist recommendation, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Your pharmacy may still need to verify it.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
